If personal information, credentials, or other sensitive material is exposed
in this repository inadvertently, do not use or redistribute it. Report it
privately in accordance with SECURITY.md and, subject to any legal preservation
obligation, delete copies under your control.

6. Contributions and chain of title

The Repository Owner does not accept an external contribution for incorporation
into Owner Material unless, before merge or incorporation, the contributor and
the Repository Owner execute a separate written agreement that:

- identifies both parties by their legal names and identifies the contribution;
- assigns to the Repository Owner all assignable intellectual-property rights
  in the contribution, including present and future copyright to the extent
  permitted by law;
- contains any moral-rights consent or waiver permitted by applicable law;
- confirms the contributor has authority to make the assignment; and
- identifies all Third-Party Material and material generated or suggested by an
  artificial-intelligence system.

Opening an issue or pull request, authoring a commit, accepting this notice, or
making material publicly visible does not by itself transfer ownership. A
repository notice cannot retroactively assign rights in an existing
contribution. See CONTRIBUTING.md.

If an external contribution is incorporated without the required assignment,
then, to the extent a valid contract is formed and unless a separate agreement
provides otherwise, the contributor grants the Repository Owner a perpetual,
irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, transferable, sublicensable,
non-exclusive licence to use, reproduce, modify, adapt, create derivative works
from, publish, distribute, communicate, display, perform, license,
commercialise, and otherwise exploit that contribution for any purpose. This
fallback licence does not transfer ownership.

7. Artificial-intelligence material

Material generated or suggested by an artificial-intelligence system may not
be copyrightable, may not be unique, and may resemble third-party material.
Provider terms, a provider's assignment of its rights, or the Repository
Owner's possession of output does not by itself prove human authorship,
originality, non-infringement, or exclusive ownership. The rights reservation
in this notice reaches such material only to the extent protectable rights
lawfully exist and are owned or controlled by the Repository Owner.

